Pre-existing third-party rights are NOT affected and remain with their holders;
this LICENSE governs only the original contributions of this repository and does
not grant, nor claim to grant, rights over the third-party source texts:

  * UN Model Double Taxation Convention (2017 edition): United Nations
    publication. No copyright notice in the document. Structured derivatives
    (AKN, markdown, search index) are reproduced for text-and-data-mining with
    attribution ("Source: United Nations, UN Model Double Taxation Convention
    2017") and do NOT replace the official UN text. The source PDF is never
    redistributed - fetch and hash only.

  * UN Model Double Taxation Convention (2021 edition): Copyright (C)
    United Nations 2021, all rights reserved (Sales No. E.21.XVI.1). The UN
    text-and-data-mining terms allow reproduction for non-commercial TDM with
    attribution only; the PDF itself is never redistributed.

  * Multilateral Instrument (consolidated text), Signatories and Parties, and
    the country position documents: OECD material. The documents read here carry
    no rights notice of their own - verified on the files: the Convention (49
    pages), the signatories table and the position documents print none. That
    absence is a fact about the document, not a licence: the publisher's own
    terms govern reuse, and the CC BY 4.0 default applies to content *published*
    from 1 July 2024, which these predate. Structured extraction is published
    with attribution to the publisher and a link to the original; the source PDFs
    are fetched locally and never committed.

  * OECD Model Tax Convention editions (added for the diachronic corpus): the
    rights are per document, because each printing states its own. The 1963
    draft and the 1977 Model carry a permission-and-translation clause; 1992,
    1998, 2000, 2003, 2005, 2008, 2014 and 2017 read "(c) OECD" with permission,
    "non-commercial reproduction" or Copyright Clearance Center wording - the
    2005 printing says no reproduction may be made without written permission.
    The exception is the current pair: the 2025 Update and the 2025 Full Version
    are published under **Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)** ((c) OECD
    2025 and 2026), which permits reuse with attribution. Which of the earlier
    editions this project may publish as text, and which it may use only as a
    comparative reading, is a decision it has not yet taken: each such source
    will say so in its own register entry when it enters the corpus.

  * Akoma Ntoso 3.0 XSD and related schemas: (c) OASIS Open, TC Open Repository -
    used solely for validation (vendor/akn/).

  Nothing above grants a right the holder has not granted: this appendix records
  what each document, and the publisher's terms, say about themselves.

